  discoveredBy: Smithson Tennant
  description: "Osmium (from Greek osme (\u1F40\u03C3\u03BC\u03AE) meaning \"smell\")
    is a chemical element with symbol Os and atomic number 76. It is a hard, brittle,
    bluish-white transition metal in the platinum group that is found as a trace
    element in alloys, mostly in platinum ores. Osmium is the densest naturally occurring
    element, with a density of 22.59 g/cm3."
